TAIL_WHEEL — два колеса спереди, рулевое:
TAIL_WHEEL — two wheels in front, the steering one at the back (taildragger): parked nose-up; on the takeoff run the tail rises first, then the wing lifts off (like the Astro-Cargo);
  NOSE_WHEEL — steering wheel in front (tricycle gear): sits almost level, raises the nose at liftoff speed.

Auto takeoff (autopilot/TakeoffController.h) and the ground calibration checks (control/GroundCalibration.h) depend on this.

Пишет полёт на встроенный флеш или на SD:
Records the flight to the onboard flash or to an SD card, about 20 KB/s with the bench sensor set:
  ESP32-S3 N16R8 — the "blackbox" flash partition, ~13.9 MB (partitions_blackbox.csv), ~11 minutes;
  STM32H743 — the BLACKBOX_SD_FILE file in the root of a FAT32 card (SDMMC1, 4-bit), preallocated on a PC: tools/blackbox.py sd-prepare; 64 MB — ~55 minutes;
  ESP32-C3 and the plain ESP32 — no storage, the black box is off.

Recording starts when armed with the throttle up (stick or ESC above THROTTLE_LOW_US) and captures BLACKBOX_PREROLL_MS before that. It ends BLACKBOX_POSTROLL_MS after DISARM, or when armed but the motor is stopped and the plane is still for BLACKBOX_LANDED_STOP_MS (landed or crashed, and DISARM was forgotten). Link loss, motor at zero in the air and gliding don't stop the recording.

Протокол приёмника; провод от его выхода:
Receiver protocol; the wire from its output goes to PIN_RC_RX:
IBUS — FlySky (FS-iA6B, FS-iA10B);
SBUS — FrSky, Futaba, RadioMaster, Jumper and most others;
the signal is inverted, the UART itself does the inversion;
CRSF — ExpressLRS, TBS Crossfire and Tracer.
SBUS and CRSF have 16 channels, the firmware uses the first RC_CHANNELS.

Хвостовое колесо (TAIL_WHEEL):\nхвост вв:
Tail wheel (TAIL_WHEEL):
tail up — elevator forward (no more than TD_TAIL_UP_ELEVATOR_US), the prop wash lifts the tail to pitch TD_ROLL_PITCH_DEG (slightly above the horizon): TD_PITCH_KP µs per degree to the target, easing off as it levels out, elevator back below the target; TD_PITCH_KD µs per °/s damps the jerk. The tail is up when pitch is within TD_TAIL_UP_DONE_DEG of the target; not up within TD_TAIL_UP_TIMEOUT_MS — aborted takeoff;
level run — tail wheel in the air (TD_ROLL_PITCH_KP µs per degree) for TD_ROLL_MS, with a pitot tube or GPS — until TAKEOFF_ROTATE_SPEED_MS;
liftoff — the pitch target grows at TD_ROTATE_RATE_DPS, but until liftoff is seen it stays no higher than the parked attitude minus TD_TAIL_CLEARANCE_DEG: the tail wheel won't touch the runway, the wing lifts off;
nose below TD_MIN_PITCH_DEG for longer than TAKEOFF_NOSE_DOWN_MS — the prop is near the ground.
